{"id":"src/app/api/ai-search/answer/route.ts","pkg":"src/app/api","kind":"route","lines":132,"commentLines":14,"header":["ANSWER FIRST (step 29a). I take the question and the documents the search just found (their type and id), read their text, and ask the model to answer ONLY from it, with a word-for-word quote for every fact. I return the answer ONLY if the program can prove it (src/lib/search/circularAnswer.ts). Otherwise the result is {answer: null}, and the screen shows the documents exactly as before. It is generic: it knows nothing about any particular circular. It is off unless NEXT_PUBLIC_FRONT_PATH_ANSWER_FIRST=true (404 otherwise). I trace it like every search: x-omni-* headers and one \"[front-path] answer ...\" console line with the model's exact tokens."],"symbols":[{"name":"runtime","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":21,"sig":"const runtime = \"nodejs\"","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"c77a83d2cc-runtime","usedBy":[]},{"name":"maxDuration","kind":"constant","exported":true,"line":22,"sig":"const maxDuration = 60","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"c77a83d2cc-maxDuration","usedBy":[]},{"name":"TYPES","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":24,"sig":"const TYPES: PassageType[] = [\"circular\", \"announcement\", \"holiday\"]","type":"PassageType[]","doc":[],"members":[],"items":3,"id":"c77a83d2cc-TYPES","usedBy":[]},{"name":"MAX_ITEMS","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":25,"sig":"const MAX_ITEMS = 3","type":"","doc":[],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"c77a83d2cc-MAX_ITEMS","usedBy":[]},{"name":"hits","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":28,"sig":"const hits = new Map<string, number[]>()","type":"","doc":["My plain guard against a runaway caller: 20 answers per 10 minutes per address, because each one costs model tokens."],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"c77a83d2cc-hits","usedBy":[]},{"name":"allowed","kind":"function","exported":false,"isDefault":false,"async":false,"line":29,"sig":"function allowed(ip: string, n